================================================================================
Third-party components
================================================================================

None of the projects below is vendored here. Each is installed as a dependency
(or will be, for the frameworks still to be added) and keeps its own license.
License names were read from each project's LICENSE file on GitHub on
2026-10-20 via the GitHub API (repos/{owner}/{repo}/license).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. ORBIT: Multi-Agent Safety and Security Evaluations Framework
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Authors:  Ben Hagag, William L. Anderson, Tom Taylor, Srija Chakraborty,
              Christian Schroeder de Witt (Wittlab; as cited in ORBIT's README)
    Upstream: https://github.com/wlanderson0/orbit
    Version:  1.0.3, commit 588b3035f92450ec4f0496bb8b629daa205e84c7 (tag v1.0.3)
    License:  Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE at the repository root)
    Use here: installed unmodified as a git dependency pinned to that commit.
              control_loop/adapters/orbit/ subclasses ORBIT's CollusionAttack
              and LLMMonitorDefense and registers the subclasses through
              ORBIT's own registries; no ORBIT source is copied or changed.
              ORBIT's NOTICE lists its own third-party components.

